{"id":"lem:gobler-fixed-partition-identifiability","kind":"lemma","statement":"Fix a supplied coordinate partition \(\pi_0\). For a causally minimal grouped additive-noise model on those labelled blocks satisfying the parent--child--nondescendant conditional Condition 1 restriction, the labelled block DAG is identifiable from the joint law. Equivalently, if \(R,R'\in\mathfrak G_{\pi_0}(P)\), then \(G_R=G_{R'}\).","free_symbols":["P","R","Rprime","pi0","graphOf","AGiven"],"depends_on":["def:supplied-group-class"],"status":"cited","source":{"cite":"GoblerWindischDrton2025","locator":"Corollary 1, page 1456; hypotheses in Definition 2 and Condition 1, pages 1455--1456","carrier":"logical-claim","verbatim_statement":"Let \((\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{N}, \mathcal{F}, \mathcal{G}_0)\) be a GANM with \(p\) variables. Suppose that for each node \(g \in [p]\), each parent \(j \in pa(g)\), and every set \(S\) satisfying
\begin{equation*}
pa(g) \setminus \{j\} \subseteq S \subseteq nd(g) \setminus \{g,j\},
\end{equation*}
there exists a realization \(\mathbf{x}_S \in \mathbb{R}^{\abs{S}}\) for which the conditional distribution of \(\mathbf{X}_S\) has strictly positive density with respect to the Lebesgue measure, and the triple
\begin{equation*}
\left(f_g(\mathbf{x}_{pa(g)\setminus \{j\}}, \mathbf{x}_j), P_{\mathbf{X}_j,\mathbf{X}_g\mid \mathbf{X}_S=\mathbf{x}_S}, P_{\mathbf{X}_j}\right)
\end{equation*}
satisfies Condition~\ref{cond:identifiability}. Here, the arguments \(\mathbf{x}_{pa(g)\setminus \{j\}}\) are held fixed, making the function \(f_g(\mathbf{x}_{pa(g)\setminus \{j\}}, \mathbf{x}_j)\) depend solely on \(\mathbf{x}_j\).

Then the graph \(\mathcal{G}_0\) is identifiable from the joint distribution \(P_{\mathbf{X}}\).","arxiv":"2506.05120v1","attestation":{"by":"d0-agent","note":"Checked against the authors' arXiv TeX source for Corollary 1 and its immediately preceding definitions."}},"proof_tex":""}

